{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"The interface assigns automatic joint exit to Raft, and the code explicitly allows leadership transfer to drop its exit proposal. The retry comment relies on another application callback, but transfer timeout only clears the transfer target. A new leader or later client proposal may restore progress; neither establishes progress for an idle leader that stays in office. I’ll focus the next investigation on that history.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nq=dict(question='After a committed JointImplicit change is applied while a leadership transfer is active, does Raft retain or regenerate the automatic joint-exit work when the transfer times out and the original leader continues with a responsive joint quorum but no new client proposals?',importance='A missed automatic exit can retain outgoing voters indefinitely and prevent later membership changes; it can make continued availability depend on participants intended to leave. This is a potential membership-progress defect, not an observed safety violation.',source_ids=['s-config-switch','s-confchange','src-append-reset','s-timers','s-transfer-candidate','s-leader-admission','s-node-contract','n-joint-contract','n-joint-assignment','n-enter-joint','n-autoleave-test','n-transfer-timeout'],participants=['Current leader','transfer target','remaining incoming/outgoing voter quorum','ordered application driver'],objects=['f-membership active joint configuration and AutoLeave','committed JointImplicit entry','leadTransferee','pendingConfIndex','automatic empty ConfChangeV2'],contexts=['Stable leader term with JointImplicit membership','Transfer initiated after entry commitment but before application completion','Transfer target unavailable; remaining quorum processes messages and storage','No unrelated proposals or forced election after transfer timeout'],event_paths=['Commit JointImplicit entry -> initiate transfer -> ApplyConfChange -> application completion -> automatic exit proposal rejected by leadTransferee guard -> tickHeartbeat timeout aborts transfer -> service heartbeats and Ready work'],activity_classes=['A2','A4','A5'],behavior_ids=['b-configuration','b-application','b-epoch'],fact_ids=['f-membership'],supporting_behavior_ids={'b-replication':'Commit the entry under actual voter quorum; leader proposal guard drops auto-exit during transfer.','b-persistence':'Ready persistence and completion ordering makes application callback and transfer overlap explicit.','b-api':'Public serialized calls permit transfer between commitment and completion without concurrent RawNode access.','b-election':'A new leader provides an alternative retry through its initial entry; the selected history retains the same leader.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['appliedTo retries on every later application callback, and a newly elected leader appends an empty entry that can supply such progress.','Transfer success may move responsibility to a new leader; therefore an unavailable transfer target with continued quorum is needed.','Ordinary application proposals are allowed to be dropped; automatic exit ownership is separately assigned to Raft by the JointImplicit/AutoLeave interface.','The existing TestRawNodeJointAutoLeave covers leadership loss followed by renewed campaign and application, not transfer timeout with an idle continuing leader. Its final ApplyConfChange explicitly pretends uncommitted work applied and cannot be reused as a legal prefix.'],unknowns=['Can the entire history be driven through RawNode Ready/Advance with actual quorum-produced commitment and no direct state mutation?','Does any generated acknowledgment, Ready completion or timer after transfer abort supply an alternative application callback that retries exit?','The interface gives automatic ownership but no tick bound. Need distinguish a finite delayed exit from quiescence with no enabled exit-producing work under a repeating stable heartbeat schedule.'],trigger_rationale='Source shows an assigned automatic task and a lost scheduling trigger: appliedTo submits the exit, transfer guard drops it, and timeout only clears leadTransferee. This has a clearer contract than postponed-read loss (explicitly permitted with retries), and a smaller controlled history than the disputed README persistence overlap. Execute a legal prefix with continued quorum and a no-transfer control to distinguish hidden retry work from an idle stuck joint configuration.',disposition='concrete_suspicion',preferred_check='controlled_schedule')\nsources=[dict(id='n-joint-contract',file='raftpb/raft.proto',start_line=116,end_line=150,kind='interface_statement'),dict(id='n-joint-assignment',file='raftpb/raft.proto',start_line=200,end_line=213,kind='interface_statement'),dict(id='n-enter-joint',file='raftpb/confchange.go',start_line=77,end_line=121,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='n-autoleave-test',file='rawnode_test.go',start_line=341,end_line=445,kind='test_expectation'),dict(id='n-transfer-timeout',file='raft_test.go',start_line=3106,end_line=3128,kind='test_expectation')]\ns=dict(action='continue',rationale='Select the automatic joint-exit lifecycle for focused construction and contract investigation; do not yet impose an invented finite-time liveness oracle.',question=q,sources=sources,feedback=dict(ref_ids=[x['id'] for x in sources]+['src-append-reset','s-timers','s-leader-admission'],answered='JointImplicit explicitly assigns proposing the zero configuration change to Raft, and ConfState.AutoLeave promises transition when safe. appliedTo attempts that work and acknowledges the transfer rejection case, relying on future application for retry. The transfer-timeout branch only clears leadTransferee; searched AutoLeave and abortLeaderTransfer callers show no separate timeout retry. The existing auto-leave test depends on reelection/application and includes a deliberately uncommitted final application, so it is contrary evidence for broad failure but not a compliant driver for this question.',remaining=['Construct actual three-voter commitment and an implicit joint change, overlap transfer with the leader application callback, then preserve quorum while the target remains unavailable.','Compare a no-transfer control and a later ordinary-proposal recovery probe; preserve bounded observations and avoid claiming eventual failure from a timeout alone.'],understanding='unchanged',rationale='The accepted map already distinguishes application-triggered auto-exit from timer-triggered transfer abort. New interface authority makes this a concrete Candidate without changing map meaning.'))\nopen('submission.json','w').write(json.dumps(s,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_22-35-07-etcd_raft-real-run --submission submission.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
